      "evidence": {
        "encoding": "utf-8",
        "text": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-cech-Hausdorff-quasi-compact}\nLet $X$ be a Hausdorff and quasi-compact topological space. Let\n$\\mathcal{F}$ be an abelian sheaf on $X$. Then\nthe map $\\check{H}^n(X, \\mathcal{F}) \\to H^n(X, \\mathcal{F})$ defined\nin (\\ref{equation-cech-to-cohomology}) is an isomorphism for all $n$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\nEvery open covering of $X$ has a finite subcover, which is a locally finite\nrefinement. Thus $X$ is paracompact and the result follows from\nLemma \\ref{lemma-cech-paracompact}.\n\\end{proof}\n",
        "bytes": 523,
